# Make a Dragonkin, open the eat menu, refuse to eat a food ration (Dragonkin
# have CA_BURNING_HUNGER and can only feed on blood), and reopen the eat menu.
# This exists for one assertion, inc-i9q.1: a refused meal must not destroy
# the food. Every eat-menu dump below must show the SAME ration count as the
# very first one. Before the fix (src/Item.cpp, Food::Eat) each refusal took
# one ration anyway -- 9 food rations -> 8 -> 7 -> ... -> "food ration"
# (quantity 1) after 8 refusals, on this exact seed and script.
# Run with seed 1 and tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-18.dat.
# The seed was never recorded before; established 2026-09-12.
#
# NO CHECK SCRIPT READS THESE DUMPS. This header cited
# tools/check_dragonkin_ration.sh as the enforcing check. That file has never
# existed; corrected 2026-08-17. The assertion is enforced by a person reading
# the dumps, and the measurement is recorded in the inc-i9q.1 row of
# docs/REPORTING-GATE.md. Write the check if the assertion is worth a gate.
#
# Race, subrace, class, alignment and food use @choose names, so menu
# letters moving when a list changes cannot select a different entry.
# Run with a fixed seed: attribute sets have no names, and rolls decide the
# offered feats, so attribute and feat picks stay positional. Start-menu,
# question and control keys stay counted for the reasons beside them.
# Formerly said every choice was a menu letter; corrected 2026-09-12.
#
# Dragonkin start with a random handful of food rations already in pack (part
# of the shared adventurer starting kit, not race- or class-specific gear --
# see src/Create.cpp). Seed 1 gives 9. Nothing needs to be granted by hand.

@expect "Initial Choices"
a       # Create a New Character: start menu is not a screen @choose reads.
@expect "Alter the character generation options?"
n       # No alteration: this is a yes/no question.
@expect "Explore Mode. Continue?"
y       # Continue in Explore Mode: this is a yes/no question.
@choose "Lizardfolk"
@choose "Dragonkin"
@choose "Barbarian"
@expect "Which of the five attribute sets"
a       # First attribute set: the five offered sets have no names.
@choose "Neutral"
@expect "Choose a feat"
a       # First feat: offered feats depend on attribute rolls.
a       # Second feat: offered feats depend on attribute rolls.

# Skill Manager. Three RIGHTs per skill spends everything available
# without needing to know how many ranks this character has.
@expect "Skill Manager"
# RIGHT/DOWN spend ranks and move between skills, not named choices.
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
# Finish ranks, then yes to keeping them: control and yes/no keys.
ENTER y

@expect "Your personality archetype"
y       # No match: the sixteen personality entries use [a] through [p].

# RIGHT/DOWN move the personality selection to The Manipulative Plotter.
# Personality affects only the sheet banner, so its selection is not pinned.
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
# Accept the selected archetype, then dismiss the Entry Chamber text.
ENTER y

# In the dungeon now. [e] opens "What do you want to eat?"; the only edible
# item Dragonkin start with is the food ration stack, always at [a]. Selecting
# it fires EV_EAT, CA_BURNING_HUNGER refuses it ("Only the blood of a
# carnivorous creature..."), and control returns straight to the map -- no
# further key is needed to dismiss anything. Reopen the menu and dump it, then
# repeat. Eight refusals, matching the bead's measured run.
@expect "Things in View"
e
@dump:menu01
@choose "(in pack) 9 food rations"
@expect "Things in View"
e
@dump:menu02
@choose "(in pack) 9 food rations"
@expect "Things in View"
e
@dump:menu03
@choose "(in pack) 9 food rations"
@expect "Things in View"
e
@dump:menu04
@choose "(in pack) 9 food rations"
@expect "Things in View"
e
@dump:menu05
@choose "(in pack) 9 food rations"
@expect "Things in View"
e
@dump:menu06
@choose "(in pack) 9 food rations"
@expect "Things in View"
e
@dump:menu07
@choose "(in pack) 9 food rations"
@expect "Things in View"
e
@dump:menu08
@choose "(in pack) 9 food rations"
@expect "Things in View"
e
@dump:menu09
@expect "What do you want to eat?"
ESC
@quit
